financebench_id_00438,"Does Adobe have an improving operating margin profile as of FY2022? If operating margin is not a useful metric for a company like this, then state that and explain why.",No the operating margins of Adobe have recently declined from 36.8% in FY 2021 to 34.6% in FY2022. A drop by 2.2% in a year.,ADOBE_2022_10K,domain-relevant,"As of FY2022, Adobe's operating margin profile appears to have mixed signals. The operating margin reported was $2,548 million, which decreased from $2,711 million in FY2021. Despite this decrease, the adjusted operating margin, which accounts for several factors including noncontrolling interests and unrealized gains and losses, improved from $1,721 million in FY2021 to $2,153 million in FY2022. This indicates that while the raw operating margin decreased, the adjusted operating margin, which may better reflect the underlying performance of the business, exhibited positive growth (Source: AES 2022 Annual Report).

Operating margin can be a useful but potentially limited metric for companies like Adobe, especially given its significant intangible asset base and reliance on software revenue which may have varied costs associated with its development and delivery. Adjusted operating margin is often considered to provide a clearer view of operational efficiency by excluding nonrecurring expenses and other factors that may distort the true profitability picture. Thus, in the case of Adobe, using the adjusted operating margin would be more effective for understanding its operational performance compared to just looking at the standard operating margin.",,,"[""MICROSOFT_2023_10K"", ""AES_2022_10K"", ""3M_2018_10K"", ""BESTBUY_2024Q2_10Q""]","Source: data\pdfs\AES_2022_10K.pdf

Content: 94 | 2022 Annual Report
in a lack of comparability in our results of operations and would distort the metrics that our investors use to measure us.
Adjusted Operating Margin
We define Adjusted Operating Margin as Operating Margin, adjusted for the impact of NCI, excluding (a) unrealized gains or losses related
to derivative transactions; (b) benefits and costs associated with dispositions and acquisitions of business interests, including early plant
closures; and (c) net gains at Angamos, one of our businesses in the South America SBU, associated with the early contract terminations with
Minera Escondida and Minera Spence. The allocation of HLBV earnings to noncontrolling interests is not adjusted out of Adjusted Operating
