financebench_id_01936,What is the nature & purpose of AMCOR's restructuring liability as oF Q2 of FY2023 close?,87% of the total restructuring liability is related Employee liabilities.,AMCOR_2023Q2_10Q,novel-generated,"As of June 30, 2023, Amcor's restructuring liability totaled $150 million, comprised of various costs associated with its restructuring activities. This includes $126 million attributed to employee costs, $3 million related to fixed asset costs, and $21 million for other costs.

The company's restructuring activities have been primarily driven by the need to adapt to market conditions and operational changes, including those influenced by the Russia-Ukraine conflict. Amcor anticipates that the majority of this liability will be settled within the next twelve months. The restructuring-related expenses are recorded as part of the company's other current liabilities and other non-current liabilities on its balance sheet (source: data\pdfs\AMCOR_2023_10K.pdf).

Overall, the restructuring liability reflects Amcor's ongoing efforts to enhance operational efficiency and align its cost structure with strategic business objectives.",,,"[""AMCOR_2023_10K"", ""AMCOR_2023Q2_10Q"", ""AMCOR_2020_10K"", ""AMCOR_2023Q4_EARNINGS""]","Source: data\pdfs\AMCOR_2023Q4_EARNINGS.pdf

